<RCC>
    <!--
        The dock's own appearance, offered the way res/themes.qrc offers the
        ribbon themes: built in by the applications that want it rather than
        carried by the library. The images these sheets point at stay in qxdock,
        which is why the url(:/qxdock/res/images/...) paths need no rewriting.

        Four files, and picking between them is not the application's choice:
        the _linux pair carries the extra rules an X11 desktop needs, and
        QX_DOCK_X11 is the only thing in the tree that knows which desktop that
        is. The focus_highlighting pair draws a frame around the focused dock
        widget. dockStyleSheet() takes both decisions as arguments - see it for
        why it hands the text out instead of applying it.

        Named dockstyle rather than dock so it does not read as a theme family
        beside res/themes/: these four are one look in four variants, not four
        looks to choose from, and a DockWindow without them is unstyled rather
        than differently styled.

        prefix="/" with the directory inside each <file>, which is how
        res/themes.qrc does it and why the paths come out as
        :/dockstyle/default.css. Putting "dockstyle" in the prefix as well would
        find them at :/dockstyle/dockstyle/default.css.
    -->
    <qresource prefix="/">
        <file>dockstyle/default.css</file>
        <file>dockstyle/focus_highlighting.css</file>
        <file>dockstyle/default_linux.css</file>
        <file>dockstyle/focus_highlighting_linux.css</file>
    </qresource>
</RCC>